  "assessment": "The source provides a perturbative asymptotic series for the inverse localization length in the 1D Anderson model with stealthy hyperuniform disorder. The selected cluster is the leading-order scaling family: for chi=0.1 the first nonzero Born order is W^2 giving xi ~ W^{-2}, and for chi=0.2 the second nonzero order is W^4 giving xi ~ W^{-4}. The routing hint directs extraction of the normalized leading localization-length predictor Y(q)=lim_{W_ref->0 at fixed q} xi(q*W_ref)/xi(W_ref)=q^{-p}, which cancels all unreported chi-dependent coefficients and avoids absolute W domains and figure data. The source supports the exponents p=2 (first order, chi=0.1) and p=4 (second order, chi=0.2) via the perturbation theory statements and the explicit second-order expression. The normalized predictor is a theoretical leading asymptotic quantity, not a finite-size numerical xi. The source does not provide a continuous W domain for the absolute xi, so the control is the finite benchmark ratio q in [1,10] within the fixed-ratio asymptotic variable. The private branches are chi=0.1 and chi=0.2, each with distinct source-anchored fixed conditions. The ASTs are identical power(q, negative_p) with private exponents -2 and -4. No absolute coefficients, E, k0, S(2k), or numerical protocol are encoded in the oracle. The source_ambiguities array is empty because the selected cluster is unambiguous. case_authoring_ready is true.",
